<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Contest_Closed">Contest Closed</span></h2>
<p>This Contest is now closed, please pick up the bundle <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=1559">from here</a> to see all the great entries! Congratulations to the winners and the runners-up - be sure to check out the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Community%20Contest%20Catalogue" title="Community Contest Catalogue">Catalogue</a>!
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Brief">Brief</span></h2>
<p>Create a character with dialogue for use in a variety of situations including follower, questgiver and merchant. The character will have various removable lines so that modders may use them for whatever purpose they need. The contest discussion thread can be found <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://social.bioware.com/group/2535/discussion/10580/">here</a>.
</p><p>A <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Community%20Contest%203%20mini%20-%20Head%20Morph" title="Community Contest 3 mini: Head Morph">raffled mini contest</a> is also running, requiring only a character head morph. We'd love if you entered both!
</p><p><b>DEADLINE: Monday 18 October</b> - your entry must be ready for judging before midday GMT+0. It is strongly recommended you submit well before this time in case you run into troubles. Modifications to your submission are welcomed - the newest version of your entry will be judged, although modifications made after the submission date will not be judged.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Requirements">Requirements</span></h3>
<p>All entries must:
</p>
<ul><li> Reserve and use a <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Community%20Contest%20ID%20Ranges" title="Community Contest ID Ranges">StringID range</a> <b>(do this before you start)</b></li>
<li> Be tested in-game</li>
<li> Be in English (non-native accents are very welcome, perhaps give your character an exotic background?)</li>
<li> Include MRH source material and dadbdata export of all relevant resources</li>
<li> Use only 
<ul><li> DA assets (hairs, textures) </li>
<li> (optional) hairs from <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=392">More Hairstyles</a> (the agreed mod)</li>
<li> (optional) hairs/textures which are <b>your own work</b> and are <b>included with your submission</b></li></ul></li>
<li> be suitable as a follower, questgiver and merchant</li>
<li> Include branches for the compulsory dialogues (see below)</li>
<li> complete the overview section with their entry (see below)</li>
<li> Be submitted before Monday 18 October midday (GMT+0)</li></ul>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Guidelines">Guidelines</span></h3>
<p>Strong entries will:
</p>
<ul><li> Be interesting characters with compelling dialogue</li>
<li> Have voiceover with lipsynch (this is optional, but will be looked upon favourably if done well)</li>
<li> Have quality voice acting, with attention paid to audio quality</li>
<li> Tweak FaceFX to give natural and emotive expressions</li>
<li> Set and check plot flags and approval where appropriate</li>
<li> Include dialogues to use the character in many situations (see suggestions below). The more versatile the character, the better.</li>
<li> Be usable in DA canon, or be canon inspecific, to allow them to be used in any module.</li></ul>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Allowable">Allowable</span></h3>
<p>Entries may:
</p>
<ul><li> Include custom textures/hairs (please only <b>your own</b> work though)</li>
<li> Include more than one character if they are relevant to one another as one submission (ex. brother/sister to be met together)</li>
<li> Multiple entries are always allowed unless stated otherwise</li>
<li> An entry may contain collaborative work (one person voices, the other person creates the character, for example)</li></ul>
<p>In the case of <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=392">More Hairstyles</a>, please only state it as a requirement and do not include any of the files. You do not need permission (just don't share the files)... it is the responsibility of the end-user to ensure they have the More Hairstyles mod.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Disallowable">Disallowable</span></h3>
<ul><li> For this contest, please <b>do not use other peoples mods</b> except <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=392">More Hairstyles</a> and anything which is <b>your own</b> work and is included.</li></ul>
<p><br />
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Groups_and_Prizes">Groups and Prizes</span></h2>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Groups">Groups</span></h3>
<p>This contest has only one group.
</p>
<ul><li> 1st place - 15 points, chooses first</li>
<li> 2nd place - 10 points, chooses second</li>
<li> 3rd place - 5 points, chooses third</li>
<li> Best Newcomer - 3 points (unless 1st, 2nd or 3rd place)</li>
<li> All other entries meeting requirements - 1 point</li></ul>
<p>To receive an "entry point", your submission must meet the requirements of the contest, listed at the top of this page
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Best_Newcomer_Award">Best Newcomer Award</span></h3>
<p>Every judge may nominate one newcomer as their favourite newcomer entry. To qualify, the entrant must not have submitted to a community contest before. The winning newcomer will receive three points if they don't podium (in which case, theyll be getting more points anyway!).
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Prizes">Prizes</span></h3>
<p>Please see <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Community%20Contest%20Prizes" title="Community Contest Prizes">Community Contest Prizes</a>
