<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Saarebas_by_uberdowzen_.28Lord_Uber_Dowzen.29_-_3rd_Place">Saarebas by uberdowzen (Lord Uber Dowzen) - 3rd Place</span></h2>
<ul><li> <b><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.dragonagenexus.com/downloads/file.php?id=1827">Dragon Age Nexus Page</a></b></li></ul>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Overview_3">Overview</span></h3>
<ul><li> Primary Role: Worker - Qunari Mage/Shopkeeper</li>
<li> Race: Qunari</li>
<li> Class: Mage</li>
<li> Voiced: No</li>
<li> Quest: Errand - Find missing amulet</li></ul>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Description_3">Description</span></h3>
<p>Saarebas is a Qunari mage. He has a dark past (surprise surprise) which the PC can discover if he is used as a follower. He is also suitable as a merchant (sells magical items) and a quest giver (an errand quest to find his lost amulet).
</p><p>Notes:
</p>
<ul><li> Contains very little scripting. If the character is used in a mod the following need to be removed: Approval increases from the ends of each of the 3 steps of the in-party dialogue, line giving the PC the amulet for the quest.</li>
<li> Saarebas still needs a fair bit of work to work in a mod. You'd want to include a proper hiring scripts etc to make the approval stuff work.</li></ul>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Judges_Comments_3">Judges Comments</span></h3>
<p><b>mikemike37</b>
Fits nicely with established canon for Qunari with nods to Sten's character. Might feel a little "more of the same" though. Meets all the requirements though, so is nice to drop into any mod.
</p>
